# Copy this file to ".env" and adjust for your setup, then: docker compose up -d
#
# ── Where the data lives ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Users, per-profile state, push subscriptions and invites are stored in Postgres — the
# self-hosted Supabase running on this box. The api container joins that stack's docker network
# and talks to it by service name, so no extra port is published to the internet and no Supabase
# API key is involved. The role needs rights on this database only.
#
# Format: postgres://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE
DATABASE_URL=postgres://opengym:__DB_PASSWORD__@supabase-db:5432/opengym

# ── Where the app is served from ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Only decides whether the session cookie is marked Secure, and supplies the Web Push subject
# when no VAPID_SUBJECT is set. Sign-in is a username and a password, so — unlike the passkeys
# this replaced — changing this URL can no longer lock anyone out of their account.
ORIGIN=https://harris-excess-respect-shops.trycloudflare.com
WEB_PORT=8080

# ── Admin dashboard & invite-only signup (optional) ────────────────────────
# Admin is a flag on the account itself (users.admin in the database), so the first profile you
# create can be promoted once, and after that the admin dashboard is where it is handed out.
# ADMIN_UIDS still exists as a belt-and-braces list of ids that are treated as admins.
#
# INVITE_ONLY requires a code — generated in the admin dashboard — before a new profile can be
# created. Existing accounts keep working either way.
#
#   ADMIN_UIDS=youruserid,anotheradmin
#   INVITE_ONLY=1

# ── Session length (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# How long a sign-in lasts, in days. Default 90 — long enough that people who
# train regularly never see a login screen, short enough that a stolen cookie
# doesn't stay good forever. Lower it for an instance on the open internet,
# raise it for a private one. Only affects new sign-ins; cookies already handed
# out keep the lifetime they were issued with. Users can end every session on
# every device themselves with "Sign out everywhere" in Settings.
#
#   SESSION_DAYS=90

# ── Notifications (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Push works out of the box — nothing to set. VAPID keys are generated on first
# run and saved to ./data/vapid.json. Each user's browser reports its own
# timezone automatically, so the workout-day reminder fires at their local
# time regardless of where the server runs or where they're travelling.

# ── AI Coach (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing to set. Claude's Agent SDK and the OpenAI Codex CLI are built into the api image;
# neither path needs an API key. Enable one from Settings → Admin → AI Coach.
#
# Claude: on a trusted computer where Claude Code is installed, run `claude setup-token`, then
# paste its value into "Add CLI token". Codex: choose "Sign in with ChatGPT" and complete the
# device-code flow in a trusted browser. Codex keeps its refreshable CLI cache in ./data/codex;
# treat that directory like a password-bearing backup. The app never handles a browser OAuth
# callback. It stays off until an admin turns it on, and each profile has to consent separately.
#
# The one knob here is a kill switch: set this and the Coach reports as disabled
# everywhere regardless of what is stored, which is useful for a fleet of
# instances you do not want the feature on for.
#
#   COACH_DISABLED=1
